<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM2-ENTRY-GATE-SEQUENCING>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM2-ENTRY-GATE-SEQUENCING" ;
  triage:title "AM.2 deleted the raw-framing live path and enabled the negative guard before AL.9 proof/ledger acceptance and AM.1's frozen ledger were actually accepted" ;
  triage:description "sprint-AM2-delete-legacy-http.md's must_follow and plan-phase-am.md's Entry gate both require 'AL.9 proof/ledger acceptance and AM.1's accepted frozen ledger' before deletion begins ('AM may perform inventory and write static guards in parallel with AL, but it must not delete a live path before that proof'). docs/plans/phase-am/am1-removal-ledger.md, checked into this very branch, states in its own words: 'AM acceptance is therefore not proven and freeze remains pending' and 'AL.9 ... host activation: not-yet-activated'; six of its own AM-PLAN-004..008 critical-review checklist items are unchecked. Despite this, HttpFrameReader/http_exchange.rs have already been deleted and the raw-framing negative guard already enabled in this same branch (commit 4a35fa18). Independently confirmed by two reviewers (req-qa: ATM-QA-001/002; arch-qa: ARCH-001) and by quality-mgr's own direct read of am1-removal-ledger.md lines 1-26, 172-184 at current HEAD 46ff7c50 -- the disclaimer text is current/specific (names concrete pending items: Windows TCP benchmark, host activation, multi-platform hook-mode matrix), not stale boilerplate." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
